RL_GENERAL></INTERNET_ADDRESSES_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES></NAME_ADDRESSES_CONTACT_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><ACTIVITIES_OF_CONTRACTING_ENTITY VALUE="RAILWAY_SERVICES"></ACTIVITIES_OF_CONTRACTING_ENTITY><ACTIVITIES_OF_CONTRACTING_ENTITY VALUE="URBAN_RAILWAY_TRAMWAY_TROLLEYBUS_BUS_SERVICES"></ACTIVITIES_OF_CONTRACTING_ENTITY></CONTRACTING_ENTITY_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><OBJECT_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><DESCRIPTION_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><TITLE_CONTRACT><P>Infrastructure Training and Assessment.</P></TITLE_CONTRACT><TYPE_CONTRACT_LOCATION_W_PUB><TYPE_CONTRACT VALUE="SERVICES"></TYPE_CONTRACT><SERVICE_CATEGORY_PUB>27</SERVICE_CATEGORY_PUB></TYPE_CONTRACT_LOCATION_W_PUB><LOCATION_NUTS><LOCATION><P>Northen Ireland.</P></LOCATION><NUTS CODE="UKN0"></NUTS></LOCATION_NUTS><SHORT_DESCRIPTION><P>The Infrastructure Division is responsible for the provision, maintenance, upgrade and renewal of the fixed equipment that enables our bus and train services to operate. The Division is divided into four departments – Permanent Way (better know as track), Signalling &amp; Telecommunications, Structures and Property. We wish to secure training providers who can deliver relevant training and assessment for these departments under the following lots:</P><P>Lot 1: Permanent way – Training and competency assessment in track engineering. This ranges from basic safety during permanent way works; track maintenance plain line; switch 7 crossing; track geometry; track patrolling; managing rail breaks &amp; defects; stressing; imposing &amp; removing speed restrictions; operation of on track machines etc. This information given is not intended to be an exclusive. . We anticipate approximately 120 training days annually and would have a training requirement for 120 persons. Additional training maybe required due to technology, legalisation and working practice. For indicative budget purpose and not constituting a legal requirement as it is subject to change.</P><P>Lot 2: Signalling and Telecoms – Training and competency assessment in Signalling and Telecommunication disciplines. This ranges from basic signalling; HW1000; SMTH; TPWS; AWS: Backdrives; signal faulting; signal faulting investigation; RRI; S2; Concept 32; TD/TDM;TCP/IP; installation; MOD5 –MOD1; design and planning; testing etc. This information given is not intended to be an exclusive. We anticipate approximately 70 training days annually and would have a training requirement for 50 persons. Additional training maybe required due to technology, legalisation and working practice. For indicative budget purpose and not constituting a legal requirement as it is subject to change.</P><P>Lot 3: Health &amp; Safety/Training – for the Division This ranges from risk assessment; working safely; managing safely; accident investigation; CSR; safe use of small plant &amp; equipment; vibrating plates; kango operations; chainsaws; disc-cutters; angle grinders; safe use of woodworking machines; working at heights; first aid; fire awareness/warden; assessor training; internal verification; etc. This information given is not intended to be an exclusive. We anticipate approximately 100 training days annually and would have a training requirement for 250 persons. Additional training maybe required due to technology, legalisation and working practice. For indicative budget purpose and not constituting a legal requirement as it is subject to change.</P><P>Lot 4: N I Railway Rulebook Competencies This covers Personal Track Safety, Track Safety Co-ordinator, Lookout, Handsignalling, Engineering Supervisor, Person in Charge of Possession, Emergency Operator and Person in Charge. This information given is not intended to be an exclusive. We anticipate approximately 100 training days annually and would have a training requirement for 250 persons. There will also be a requirement to provide this service to contractors on N I Railway business. Additional training maybe required due to technology, legalisation and working practice. For indicative budget purpose and not constituting a legal requirement as it is subject to change. This Lot will only become available from the 2.6.2009. The result of the exercise will be to short listed Applicants which it is hoped will be used to short list those who will be appointed to a select list of suppliers. It is anticipated that the contract will be for three years commencing January 2009.</P></SHORT_DESCRIPTION><CPV><CPV_MAIN><CPV_CODE CODE="80500000"></CPV_CODE></CPV_MAIN><CPV_ADDITIONAL><CPV_CODE CODE="79632000"></CPV_CODE></CPV_ADDITIONAL><CPV_ADDITIONAL><CPV_CODE CODE="80510000"></CPV_CODE></CPV_ADDITIONAL><CPV_ADDITIONAL><CPV_CODE CODE="80550000"></CPV_CODE></CPV_ADDITIONAL></CPV><CONTRACT_COVERED_GPA VALUE="YES"></CONTRACT_COVERED_GPA></DESCRIPTION_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES></OBJECT_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><PROCEDURES_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><TYPE_PROCEDURE_AWARD><PT_NEGOTIATED_WITH_COMPETITION></PT_NEGOTIATED_WITH_COMPETITION></TYPE_PROCEDURE_AWARD><F06_AWARD_CRITERIA_CONTRACT_UTILITIES_INFORMATION><PRICE_AWARD_CRITERIA PRICE="MOST_ECONOMICALLY_TENDER"></PRICE_AWARD_CRITERIA><NO_ELECTRONIC_AUCTION></NO_ELECTRONIC_AUCTION></F06_AWARD_CRITERIA_CONTRACT_UTILITIES_INFORMATION><ADMINISTRATIVE_INFO_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><REFERENCE_NUMBER_ATTRIBUTED><P>001/0376/08</P></REFERENCE_NUMBER_ATTRIBUTED><PREVIOUS_PUBLICATION_INFORMATION_NOTICE_F6><PREVIOUS_PUBLICATION_EXISTS_F6><CNT_NOTICE_INFORMATION><CNT_NOTICE_INFORMATION_S CHOICE="SIMPLIFIED_CONTRACT_NOTICE_DPS"></CNT_NOTICE_INFORMATION_S><NOTICE_NUMBER_OJ>2008/S 188-249458</NOTICE_NUMBER_OJ><DATE_OJ><DAY>27</DAY><MONTH>09</MONTH><YEAR>2008</YEAR></DATE_OJ></CNT_NOTICE_INFORMATION><NO_OTHER_PREVIOUS_PUBLICATION></NO_OTHER_PREVIOUS_PUBLICATION></PREVIOUS_PUBLICATION_EXISTS_F6></PREVIOUS_PUBLICATION_INFORMATION_NOTICE_F6></ADMINISTRATIVE_INFO_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES></PROCEDURES_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><AWARD_CONTRACT_CONTRACT_AWARD_UTILITIES><AWARD_AND_CONTRACT_VALUE><CONTRACT_NO>1</CONTRACT